# Barefoot and Badass: A Field Guide to Questionable Decisions and Unexpected Survival

An interactive scrapbook-style field guide documenting funny, chaotic, and mildly questionable life experiences. The project combines storytelling, visual design, and responsive web development into a humorous survival guide format.

## Project Goal

The goal of this project was to create an interactive webpage that felt playful, personal, and visually unique while practicing HTML, CSS positioning, Flexbox, image layering, navigation, and responsive design.

## Features

- Interactive sidebar navigation
- Scrollable “field guide” story sections
- Scrapbook-inspired visuals and textures
- Custom illustrations and themed imagery
- Portfolio and case study buttons
- Responsive mobile version with icon navigation
- Separate case study reflection page

## Tools Used

- HTML5
- CSS3
- Flexbox
- Media Queries
- GitHub Codespaces
- GitHub Pages
- Figma (planning and layout design)
- Co-pilot (to make sure the WHOLE page was working...until it erased all the things) 
- ChatGPT to ask for help when I couldn't figure out what was breaking, and why.

## Design Decisions

I wanted the website to feel like a handmade scrapbook mixed with a humorous survival manual. Paper textures, corkboard elements, handwritten typography, and layered visuals were used to make the guide feel personal and chaotic rather than polished or corporate.

The navigation was designed like labeled field guide tabs to reinforce the playful tone.

## Technical Challenges

One of the biggest challenges was positioning layered images and maintaining spacing across screen sizes. Desktop positioning worked visually but caused issues when adapting to mobile layouts.

This was solved through media queries, simplifying mobile layouts, changing navigation into icons, and restructuring sections to stack vertically.

## Responsive Design Strategy

The desktop version uses a left sidebar navigation and layered scrapbook elements.

The mobile version:
- hides decorative desktop elements
- replaces navigation labels with icon buttons
- switches to a mobile title image
- stacks content vertically for easier scrolling

